{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/50000-your-house-rules","id":50000,"title":"Your House Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-15T12:54:19-08:00","id":50000,"title":"Your House Rules","content":"Can any of you who have actual GM experience with Geist post your &quot;House Rules&quot;. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T15:24:08-08:00","id":51104,"title":"","content":"Three main HRs<br /> <br /> 1) You cannot use powers through Boneyard except Boneyard Powers.<br /> <br /> Reason: Being able to use powers through boneyard not only makes it an ideal method for attacking foes (as opposed to a very, very expensive one) but makes investigation even less important if they can not only superficially search an area but also use Oracle there. While Shroud and Caul are not a big deal though Boneyard, Pit, Marionette, Oracle, and Curse can be crazy, for different reasons.<br /> <br /> 2) Oracle returns a Plasm if 5 successes are gained, like Boneyard<br /> <br /> Reason: Oracle is used often, and this helps make it less punishing. Of course, individual powers do not benifet from this.<br /> <br /> 3) The 9 again on Caul activation for an exceptional success also applies to the activation roll.<br /> <br /> Reason: Very, very few Caul powers benefit from this ability, and none of those were, at least the first couple years, possessed by Caul users. This allows it to be of some use to all. Essentially, if at least 5 successes are gained, the Bound's player can reroll 9s on activation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T20:41:42-08:00","id":51345,"title":"","content":"I have a few, but their reasons are a touch less good than the Baron's.<br /> <br /> 1.) The Stigmatic Rage, when used on a Vampire, damages Vitae. However, penalties directly biology based no longer apply. The storyteller may ask for a fear frenzy roll with a brutal enough application.<br /> <i>The reason for this was my player actually. She argued that since the rage rips out blood, vampire's vitae pools should be harmed like in the hedge. She wanted lethal damage as well but honestly damaging another creatures 'juice' is nasty enough. If someone else has a more satisfying answer for this I'm all ears.</i><br /> <br /> 2.) Should a Sin Eaters body be totally destroyed, she will awake with her caul at the nearest crossroads. Should a Sin Eater's body be trapped but intact, the geist will free them in a similar fashion to the elemental Oracles and binding fluffs.<br /> [i]My players have done some <b>really</b> creative things to other Bound. And have had some creative things done to them because I allow PC on PC conflict. I didn't have an answer for what happened in 'fate worse than death' situations so I made some quick calls that stuck. Why crossroads? I thought they were cool and death oriented and they stuck.<br /> <br /> 3.) Sin Eaters dreams are always interactions with their geist. Whether this be blatant and direct or some infecting of its essence into other dreams or even experiencing one of its dreams, doesn't matter; the geist is always felt.<br /> <i>My only game right now is heavy crossover, and I felt that this was a nice touch for a Sin Eaters dreams. No mechanical benefits, I just felt this was better than the fluff in the threshold writeups.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1804-b-fox","name":"B.Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:46:25-08:00","id":53925,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'de went and thought a great deal about implementing some of the rules from Inferno, regarding The Posessed.<br /> Theres alot of stuff there regarding how hard it sucks, to have another person constantly try to dictate what you do, such as needing to roll something like Resolve+Compure to prevent being compelled to perform a certain action. Theres also some nifty benefits, like a secoundary willpower pool to draw from, to repressent the strenght of two merged minds.<br /> I've yet to implement them fully, as theres a few conversions to get down, but i'm certainly going to try it when i find the time to figure it all out, and I recommend giving that book a read. Its worth your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}